    {tutorialOpen&&<div className="tutorial-backdrop" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="ONE BRAIN guided tutorial"><div className="tutorial-window"><div className="tutorial-top"><div className="tutorial-brand"><BrainCircuit size={18}/> ONE BRAIN · GUIDED TOUR</div><button className="modal-close" onClick={()=>{setTutorialDone(true);setTutorialOpen(false);setTutorialStep(0);}}> <XCircle size={18}/> </button></div><div className="tutorial-progress"><span style={{width:(((tutorialStep+1)/9)*100)+"%"}}/></div><div className="tutorial-count">STEP {tutorialStep+1} OF 9</div><div className="tutorial-symbol"><BookOpen size={28}/></div><h2>{["Welcome to ONE BRAIN","Your workspace and navigation","AI Chat and conversations","AI Studio and model providers","PC Control and safe computer actions","Network and FORD MDT","Diagnostics and experimental tools","Settings, privacy and updates","You're ready to use ONE BRAIN"][tutorialStep]}</h2><p>{["ONE BRAIN brings AI chat, model providers, desktop tools and device information into one workspace. This walkthrough introduces each area. You can skip it now and replay it at any time from Settings.","Use the left navigation to switch between Dashboard, PC Control, AI Chat, AI Studio, Network, Diagnostics, Activity and Settings. The interface keeps your workspace and preferences together.","AI Chat is where you can ask your selected model questions. Start a new conversation, continue an existing thread, search your history, pin important chats and export conversations when needed.","AI Studio and Settings let you configure a compatible provider endpoint, API key and model ID. API calls may cost money depending on your provider. You can also use a local Ollama model if it is installed and configured.","PC Control is a permission-based desktop assistant. Describe the task, review what it is doing and stop it when needed. Capabilities depend on the operating system and available permissions; it is not unrestricted access to every app or file.","Network shows devices detected on your local network. FORD MDT is a separate interface area and may require its own access. Network discovery is best-effort and cannot guarantee every device will appear.","Diagnostics provides system and hardware information. CSI Radar is experimental and currently marked Coming Soon; do not treat it as a working radar or verified sensing system yet.","Settings contains provider credentials, appearance options, sound controls and Software Updates. Updates are checked against official project releases. Keep your API keys private and use provider spending limits. On macOS, automatic installation requires a properly signed app build.","That's the walkthrough. You can revisit it from Settings → Guided App Tutorial. Some modules are still under development, and available features differ between Windows, macOS and mobile. Thanks for using ONE BRAIN."][tutorialStep]}</p><div className="tutorial-footer"><button className="outline-btn" onClick={()=>{setTutorialDone(true);setTutorialOpen(false);setTutorialStep(0);}}>Skip tutorial</button><div className="tutorial-nav">{tutorialStep>0&&<button className="outline-btn" onClick={()=>setTutorialStep(n=>Math.max(0,n-1))}>Back</button>}{tutorialStep<8?<button className="run-btn" onClick={()=>setTutorialStep(n=>Math.min(8,n+1))}>Next <ChevronRight size={15}/></button>:<button className="run-btn" onClick={()=>{setTutorialDone(true);setTutorialOpen(false);setTutorialStep(0);}}>Finish tutorial <Check size={15}/></button>}</div></div></div></div>}
